Installation:
=============

Copy the Puzzle.opa file into any \APP directory and install
in the usual way, using Psion-i from the system screen.

Copy the Bart.pic file into any \PIC directory. This can be
loaded into the puzzle and used as a picture in place of the
numbers 1 to 15. The file can actually be stored anywhere,
but remember where you put it when you try and load it into
the program!

Puzzle v0.12 for psion 3a
=========================

Improvements over version 0.02
------------------------------
An option has been added to load a grey/black bitmap pair
from a PIC file and use it as the puzzle picture, in place
of the numbers 1 to 15.
A sample PIC file is included (of Bart Simpson!).

New options available:

Psion-l : Load a pic file
Psion-w : Wipe the puzzle (return to numbers)

NOTE: The PIC file MUST be a black/grey bitmap pair, and
both black and grey bitmaps must be 128x128 pixels.

There are slight differences in the screen display in this version.

Later versions may include larger puzzle areas and more pieces.

Puzzle v0.02 for psion 3a
=========================

This version is a simple puzzle appication for the psion 3a.

The following options are available:

Psion-r : Create a random puzzle layout (not always solvable (?))
Psion-s : Shuffle the puzzle (always solvable)
Psion-x : Exit the game
Psion-c : Clear the puzzle
Psion-v : Show version number

You may have to shuffle or randomize the puzzle more than
once to create a completely disarranged puzzle.

Move a piece using the cursor keys - a piece will move in the
direction of the cursor key you press if possible.
A whole row/column can be moved in one go using shift-cursor keys.

